Here are the named characters/people in the story, grouped by how they appear:

## Main named characters
1. **Edward Milsom** — the “variable man” brought from the early twentieth century.  
2. **Eric Paddington** — Security Commissioner.  
3. **Peter Gibson** — director of the Military Designs Department.  
4. **Margaret Wheeler** — President of the Council.  
5. **Jeremy** — lab organizer associated with the SRB machines.  
6. **Joseph Dixon** — Security officer.  
7. **E. Fredman** — Histo-Research official who orders the time bubble brought back manually.  
8. **Goodwin** — chief official of Histo-Research.  
9. **Fleet Commander Tucker** — military commander involved in the war planning.  
10. **Director Blackwell** — official of Federal Stockpile Conservation who confronts Milsom.  
11. **Steven** — the boy whose inter-system vidsender is broken.  
12. **Earl** — the boy who breaks Steven’s vidsender.  
13. **Jennifer Preston** — the girl with Steven and Earl.  
14. **Richard Hurst** — Steven’s father, an electrical engineer.

## Named people mentioned but not active in the main action
15. **Douglas West** — the inventor whose earlier faster-than-light research made Icarus possible; he is long dead.  
16. **Mrs. Norris** — mentioned incidentally as the owner of the back yard the children jump into.  
17. **Vice-Commander Dickerson** — mentioned as receiving orders to end the battle.

## Named object/personified entity
18. **Icarus** — the faster-than-light bomb. It is called “he” at times, but it is not a human character.

If historical figures mentioned in passing are also counted, the story also names **Edison**, **Pasteur**, **Burbank**, and the **Wright brothers**, though they are not characters in the narrative.


